{
    "background_story": "Jericho was a majestic inland taipan, a species known scientifically as Oxyuranus microlepidotus. Found in the arid deserts of central Australia, Jericho ruled the sandy dunes with stealth and precision. His venom was potent, capable of taking down prey with a single strike. Yet, Jericho was not a mindless killer. He was a calculated hunter, using his acute senses to track his quarry. Despite his fearsome reputation, Jericho had a peculiar fondness for a nearby waterhole, where he would often bask in the sun's warmth. Locals avoided the area, whispering tales of the deadly Oxyuranus that lurked beneath the rocks. But Jericho was a creature of habit, returning to his favorite spot every day, a testament to the enduring power of this desert monarch.",
